diff --git a/docs/ops/observability.md b/docs/ops/observability.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..96613a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/observability.md
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# Observability lanes
+
+Application output is split into three explicit lanes. Pick the lane by asking
+**who needs this information and what should they do with it?**
+
+| Lane | Destination | Audience | Use it for |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Archive | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily, 14 days) | Developers / support | Normal application logs from `debug` through `error`: request context, queue activity, handled failures, diagnostics. |
+| Audit | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily, 90 days, `info`+) | Security / operations / finance | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" records: membership role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, administrative actions. |
+| Alert | Discord incoming webhook | On-call operators | Incidents that need a human now: exhausted job retries, failing payment-gateway webhooks, plan limits blocking a real entity. |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. **Does a person need to be paged right now?**
+   Use the alert lane via `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert`. Do not log an alert and
+   hope someone reads it.
+2. **Would we need this record months from now to explain a change or blocked
+   attempt?**
+   Use the audit lane: `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])`.
+3. **Otherwise**
+   Use the normal `Log` facade. It writes to the archive lane through the
+   `stack`/`daily` channels.
+
+### Rules of thumb
+
+- Alerts are explicit, not automatic. An exception handler, job, webhook, or
+  domain service must decide that an incident is page-worthy and call the
+  notifier itself.
+- Discord is **not** a Monolog channel. Never add a `discord` logging channel
+  and never route `Log::error()` to the webhook. That would page on every
+  ordinary error and turn the alert lane into noise.
+- Audit entries are append-only records, not debugging output. Include the
+  actor, target entity, action, and before/after values where relevant.
+- Archive logs are rotated separately from audit logs, so keep audit records
+  out of `laravel.log`.
+
+## Sending an ops alert
+
+The notifier has no constructor dependencies, so it can be resolved from the
+container or instantiated directly:
+
+```php
+use App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert;
+
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Webhook retries exhausted',
+    'The Asaas payment webhook failed after all retries.',
+    [
+        'queue' => 'asaas-webhooks',
+        'entity_id' => 42,
+    ],
+);
+```
+
+The message text is `title`, then `message`, then one `key=value` line per
+context entry, joined by newlines. It is truncated to 1800 characters.
+
+Context values are redacted before sending:
+
+- Sensitive keys (`password`, `token`, `secret`, `authorization`,
+  `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook`) become `[redacted]`.
+- Any string containing a `Bearer <credential>` value becomes `[redacted]`.
+- Nested arrays follow the same rules recursively and are rendered as JSON.
+
+The notifier never throws. When the webhook is unset it does nothing. When
+Discord returns a non-2xx response or the HTTP request fails, it writes an
+`error` entry to the archive log instead. The webhook URL/token is scrubbed from
+those log entries.
+
+## Configuration
+
+```dotenv
+LOG_STACK=daily
+LOG_DAILY_DAYS=14
+LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL=info
+LOG_AUDIT_DAYS=90
+DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
+```
+
+Leave `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` empty to disable Discord alerts entirely. The test
+environment pins `LOG_STACK=daily` in `phpunit.xml` so it does not depend on a
+local `.env` file.
